) Display Text using String Literals
AIM
To write a React program to display text using string (template) literals.
PROGRAM (App.jsx)
function App() {
 const name = "Ravi";
 const college = "KSRMCE";
 return <h1>{`Hello ${name}, welcome to ${college}!`}</h1>;
}
export default App;
OUTPUT
● ● ● localhost:5173
Hello Ravi, welcome to KSRMCE!
Output in browser
KEY POINTS
• String literals use backticks ( ` ` ), not quotes.
• ${variable} → puts the variable's value inside the text.
• In JSX, wrap it in { } so React treats it as JavaScript.
